    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The full suite passes: **52 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe specification required rejecting owner requests with a 400 when the email domain is on a disposable-domain blocklist (`mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com`).\n\nThe codebase already funnels all owner email handling through `OwnerEmail.normalize(...)`, called by both the create pipeline (`ValidateOwnerFields` for `POST /api/owners`) and the update pipeline (`ValidateOwner` for `PUT /api/owners/{ownerId}`). It already throws the checked `InvalidEmailException` for syntactically invalid addresses, and `InvalidEmailExceptionHandler` maps that to a 400.\n\nSo the change was a single, well-placed addition in `OwnerEmail.java`:\n- Added a `DISPOSABLE_DOMAINS` set with the three blocklisted domains.\n- After the existing syntax check and lower-casing, it extracts the domain and throws `InvalidEmailException` if it's on the blocklist.\n\nBecause normalization runs in both create and update pipelines, disposable-domain emails are now rejected with 400 on both endpoints, and the case-insensitivity is handled by comparing against the already-lower-cased value. The new `Cp38Tests` acceptance test and all 52 existing tests pass.",
